# Greenstone Management System — environment example (root)
#
# This file documents where environment configuration lives.
# It does not hold any values itself.
#
# The frontend and backend use separate environment files:
#
#   frontend/.env.example  ->  copy to  frontend/.env.local
#   backend/.env.example   ->  copy to  backend/.env
#
# Rules:
# - Never commit a real .env file.
# - Never place secrets in a frontend variable.
# - Only NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are exposed to the browser.
# - Development, test, staging, and production use separate values.
